      "text": "Project-Github-Link: https://github.com/sunnysavita10/ecomm-prod-assistant\n\n\nThese are all the commands which you need to run on your command prompt\n\nWrite python on your terminal\nIf you have python then no need to install it\n uv --version\nIf you are not able to get the version\nPip install uv\nimport shutil\nprint(shutil.which(\"uv\"))\n \n 6. Uv init <my-project-name>\n7. uv pip list\n \n8. uv python list\nuv venv myenvp10 --python cpython-3.10.18-windows-x86_64-none\nuv venv myenv --python cpython-3.11.13-windows-x86_64-none\nuv venv <your-env-namne> --python <your-python-version>\nNote: please use either 3.10 or 3.11 or 3.12\nCommand Prompt (CMD)  .\\<your-env-nanme>\\Scripts\\activate.bat\nGit Bash ya WSL terminal  or MAC Terminal:\nsource <your-env-nanme>/Scripts/activate\n\n18. If your git is asking for login to publish the repo execute this below\ncommand\ngit config --global user.name \"Your Name\"\ngit config --global user.email \"your-email@example.com\"\ngit config commit.gpgsign false\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Project-Github-Link: https://github.com/sunnysavita10/ecomm-prod-assistant\n\n\nThese are all the commands which you need to run on your command prompt\n\nWrite python on your terminal\nIf you have python then no need to install it\n uv --version\nIf you are not able to get the version\nPip install uv\nimport shutil\nprint(shutil.which(\"uv\"))\n \n 6. Uv init <my-project-name>\n7. uv pip list\n \n8. uv python list\nuv venv myenvp10 --python cpython-3.10.18-windows-x86_64-none\nuv venv myenv --python cpython-3.11.13-windows-x86_64-none\nuv venv <your-env-namne> --python <your-python-version>\nNote: please use either 3.10 or 3.11 or 3.12\nCommand Prompt (CMD)  .\\<your-env-nanme>\\Scripts\\activate.bat\nGit Bash ya WSL terminal  or MAC Terminal:\nsource <your-env-nanme>/Scripts/activate\n\n18. If your git is asking for login to publish the repo execute this below command\ngit config --global user.name \"Your Name\"\ngit config --global user.email \"your-email@example.com\"\ngit config commit.gpgsign false\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
